linux bash script for automatic keyboard backlight on laptops
oneloopsol.com

Created in co-operation with ChatGPT, no edits by me.

Intent is a laptop brand independent script for automatic keyboard backlighting

Turns off the backlight after 20 seconds (change parameter in script, then run './auto-kbd-brightness install' again)
Turns backlight automatically back on, on any keypress (even "passive" keys Ctrl, Shift, Alt)
  Does not turn on backlight if screen brightness is above 200 (i.e. 50%)

Not tested that much, but it works for me. I immediately like it.

Usage:

chmod +x auto-kbd-backlight
./auto-kbd-backlight install
